+# Delivery Plan
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Milestone | Start | End |
+|---|---|---|
+| kickoff | 2026-08-24 | 2026-08-26 |
+| requirements | 2026-08-27 | 2026-09-07 |
+| architecture | 2026-09-08 | 2026-09-14 |
+| build-core | 2026-09-15 | 2026-10-01 |
+| build-integrations | 2026-10-02 | 2026-10-15 |
+| hardening | 2026-10-16 | 2026-10-23 |
+| acceptance | 2026-10-26 | 2026-10-29 |
+| launch | 2026-10-30 | 2026-11-02 |
+
+## Countdown
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Business days until kickoff | 5 |
+| Total business days | 48 |
+
+## Notes
+
+The plan runs eight milestones back-to-back with no slack between them, from
+kickoff on 2026-08-24 through launch ending 2026-11-02 — 48 business days
+(about 9.5 calendar weeks) of scheduled work, starting 5 business days from
+today.
+
+Three company holidays fall inside the schedule and push milestone end dates
+out by one business day each: 2026-08-31 lands during `requirements`,
+2026-09-25 during `build-core`, and 2026-10-12 during `build-integrations`.
+The longest stretches are `build-core` (12 days) and `build-integrations` (9
+days), which together make up nearly half the plan — any slippage there has
+the most schedule risk. `hardening` ends on a Friday (2026-10-23), so
+`acceptance` doesn't pick up until the following Monday (2026-10-26).
